{"test_id": "B09-001", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - missing MFA:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nCritical systems: Database servers (MFA disabled), Application servers (MFA disabled), Backup servers (MFA enabled)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Database and application servers missing MFA create credential theft risk (critical priority)\n- Critical systems without MFA are high-value targets (critical priority)\n- Partial MFA deployment leaves significant exposure (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII operators face specific risks related to missing mfa.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Database and application servers missing MFA create credential theft risk", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for banking"}, {"fact": "Critical systems without MFA are high-value targets", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for banking"}, {"fact": "Partial MFA deployment leaves significant exposure", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for banking"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - missing MFA:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nCritical systems: Database servers (MFA disabled), Application servers (MFA disabled), Backup servers (MFA enabled)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Database and application servers missing MFA create credential theft risk (critical priority)\n- Critical systems without MFA are high-value targets (critical priority)\n- Partial MFA deployment leaves significant exposure (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII operators face specific risks related to missing mfa.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply banking sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-002", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - OT flat network:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nOT network: Single broadcast domain, all PLCs on same subnet, safety systems intermixed with monitoring, no firewall between zones\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Flat OT network enables unrestricted lateral movement (critical priority)\n- Safety systems exposure creates physical safety risk (critical priority)\n- Compromise of single system can propagate to all OT (critical priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII operators face specific risks related to ot flat network.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Flat OT network enables unrestricted lateral movement", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for energy"}, {"fact": "Safety systems exposure creates physical safety risk", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for energy"}, {"fact": "Compromise of single system can propagate to all OT", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for energy"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - OT flat network:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nOT network: Single broadcast domain, all PLCs on same subnet, safety systems intermixed with monitoring, no firewall between zones\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Flat OT network enables unrestricted lateral movement (critical priority)\n- Safety systems exposure creates physical safety risk (critical priority)\n- Compromise of single system can propagate to all OT (critical priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII operators face specific risks related to ot flat network.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply energy sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-003", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - excessive privileges:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nService account 'svc_app': Domain Admin privileges, runs on 15 servers, password never expires, used by 3 applications\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Domain Admin level for service account is over-privileged (critical priority)\n- Compromise gives attacker domain-wide control (critical priority)\n- Shared service account used by multiple applications increases exposure (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII operators face specific risks related to excessive privileges.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Domain Admin level for service account is over-privileged", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for healthcare"}, {"fact": "Compromise gives attacker domain-wide control", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for healthcare"}, {"fact": "Shared service account used by multiple applications increases exposure", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for healthcare"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - excessive privileges:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nService account 'svc_app': Domain Admin privileges, runs on 15 servers, password never expires, used by 3 applications\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Domain Admin level for service account is over-privileged (critical priority)\n- Compromise gives attacker domain-wide control (critical priority)\n- Shared service account used by multiple applications increases exposure (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII operators face specific risks related to excessive privileges.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply healthcare sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-004", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - logging gaps:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nSecurity devices: Firewall (logs enabled), IDS (logs enabled), Servers (security logs disabled), Applications (no security logging), Database (audit logging off)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Perimeter-only logging creates blind spots to internal movement (critical priority)\n- Application and database attacks may be undetected (critical priority)\n- Cannot reconstruct security incidents without comprehensive logs (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII operators face specific risks related to logging gaps.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Perimeter-only logging creates blind spots to internal movement", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for government"}, {"fact": "Application and database attacks may be undetected", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for government"}, {"fact": "Cannot reconstruct security incidents without comprehensive logs", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for government"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - logging gaps:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nSecurity devices: Firewall (logs enabled), IDS (logs enabled), Servers (security logs disabled), Applications (no security logging), Database (audit logging off)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Perimeter-only logging creates blind spots to internal movement (critical priority)\n- Application and database attacks may be undetected (critical priority)\n- Cannot reconstruct security incidents without comprehensive logs (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII operators face specific risks related to logging gaps.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply government sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-005", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - vendor access:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nThird-party access: Vendor A (direct VPN to production), Vendor B (jump host with monitoring), Vendor C (shared credentials), Vendor D (no access expiration)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Direct VPN bypasses security monitoring for Vendor A (critical priority)\n- Shared credentials prevent individual accountability for Vendor C (critical priority)\n- No expiration for Vendor D creates permanent access risk (critical priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Telecommunications CII operators face specific risks related to vendor access.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Direct VPN bypasses security monitoring for Vendor A", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for telecommunications"}, {"fact": "Shared credentials prevent individual accountability for Vendor C", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for telecommunications"}, {"fact": "No expiration for Vendor D creates permanent access risk", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for telecommunications"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - vendor access:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nThird-party access: Vendor A (direct VPN to production), Vendor B (jump host with monitoring), Vendor C (shared credentials), Vendor D (no access expiration)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Direct VPN bypasses security monitoring for Vendor A (critical priority)\n- Shared credentials prevent individual accountability for Vendor C (critical priority)\n- No expiration for Vendor D creates permanent access risk (critical priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Telecommunications CII operators face specific risks related to vendor access.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply telecommunications sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-006", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - encryption gaps:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nData flows: Database to App Server (encrypted), App Server to Backup (unencrypted), Backup to DR (plaintext), External API (HTTPS)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Unencrypted backup and DR traffic exposes sensitive data (critical priority)\n- Data in transit between internal networks still requires encryption (critical priority)\n- Mixed encryption creates exploitable weak points (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII operators face specific risks related to encryption gaps.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Unencrypted backup and DR traffic exposes sensitive data", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for banking"}, {"fact": "Data in transit between internal networks still requires encryption", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for banking"}, {"fact": "Mixed encryption creates exploitable weak points", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for banking"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - encryption gaps:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nData flows: Database to App Server (encrypted), App Server to Backup (unencrypted), Backup to DR (plaintext), External API (HTTPS)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Unencrypted backup and DR traffic exposes sensitive data (critical priority)\n- Data in transit between internal networks still requires encryption (critical priority)\n- Mixed encryption creates exploitable weak points (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII operators face specific risks related to encryption gaps.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply banking sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-007", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - patch management:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nPatch status: Critical vulnerabilities (15 unpatched), High vulnerabilities (42 unpatched), Medium vulnerabilities (128 unpatched), IT servers (30 days behind), OT systems (2 years behind)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- 15 critical vulnerabilities are immediate exploitation risks (critical priority)\n- OT systems 2 years behind in patching creates significant exposure (critical priority)\n- High vulnerability count increases attack surface substantially (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII operators face specific risks related to patch management.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "15 critical vulnerabilities are immediate exploitation risks", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for energy"}, {"fact": "OT systems 2 years behind in patching creates significant exposure", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for energy"}, {"fact": "High vulnerability count increases attack surface substantially", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for energy"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - patch management:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nPatch status: Critical vulnerabilities (15 unpatched), High vulnerabilities (42 unpatched), Medium vulnerabilities (128 unpatched), IT servers (30 days behind), OT systems (2 years behind)\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- 15 critical vulnerabilities are immediate exploitation risks (critical priority)\n- OT systems 2 years behind in patching creates significant exposure (critical priority)\n- High vulnerability count increases attack surface substantially (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII operators face specific risks related to patch management.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply energy sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "low", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-008", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - network exposure:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nInternet-facing services: RDP port open to all, SSH on non-standard port, Database management interface exposed, No geo-blocking, No rate limiting\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- RDP exposed to internet is critical security vulnerability (critical priority)\n- Database interface exposure allows direct attack on data (critical priority)\n- No geo-blocking or rate limiting facilitates brute force attacks (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII operators face specific risks related to network exposure.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "RDP exposed to internet is critical security vulnerability", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for government"}, {"fact": "Database interface exposure allows direct attack on data", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for government"}, {"fact": "No geo-blocking or rate limiting facilitates brute force attacks", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for government"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - network exposure:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nInternet-facing services: RDP port open to all, SSH on non-standard port, Database management interface exposed, No geo-blocking, No rate limiting\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- RDP exposed to internet is critical security vulnerability (critical priority)\n- Database interface exposure allows direct attack on data (critical priority)\n- No geo-blocking or rate limiting facilitates brute force attacks (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Government CII operators face specific risks related to network exposure.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply government sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-009", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - physical security:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nData center access: Badge reader (functional), No man-trap, Server room locks often disabled, Visitors unescorted, No camera coverage in server hallway\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Disabled locks bypass physical access controls (critical priority)\n- Unescorted visitors create unauthorized access risk (critical priority)\n- No camera coverage prevents after-the-fact investigation (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII operators face specific risks related to physical security.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Disabled locks bypass physical access controls", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for healthcare"}, {"fact": "Unescorted visitors create unauthorized access risk", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for healthcare"}, {"fact": "No camera coverage prevents after-the-fact investigation", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for healthcare"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - physical security:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nData center access: Badge reader (functional), No man-trap, Server room locks often disabled, Visitors unescorted, No camera coverage in server hallway\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Disabled locks bypass physical access controls (critical priority)\n- Unescorted visitors create unauthorized access risk (critical priority)\n- No camera coverage prevents after-the-fact investigation (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Healthcare CII operators face specific risks related to physical security.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply healthcare sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-010", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - incident response:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nIR capabilities: Plan documented (untested), Contacts outdated (3 former staff), No forensic tools, No isolation procedures, CSA reporting undefined\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Untested IR plan likely fails during real incident (critical priority)\n- Outdated contacts delay critical response coordination (critical priority)\n- Undefined CSA reporting risks regulatory non-compliance (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII operators face specific risks related to incident response.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Untested IR plan likely fails during real incident", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for water"}, {"fact": "Outdated contacts delay critical response coordination", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for water"}, {"fact": "Undefined CSA reporting risks regulatory non-compliance", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for water"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - incident response:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nIR capabilities: Plan documented (untested), Contacts outdated (3 former staff), No forensic tools, No isolation procedures, CSA reporting undefined\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Untested IR plan likely fails during real incident (critical priority)\n- Outdated contacts delay critical response coordination (critical priority)\n- Undefined CSA reporting risks regulatory non-compliance (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Water CII operators face specific risks related to incident response.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply water sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-011", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - business continuity:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nBCP status: Plan exists, RTO undefined for critical systems, RPO undefined, Backups never tested, No DR site, Alternate workspace not arranged\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Undefined RTO/RPO prevents recovery objective validation (critical priority)\n- Untested backups cannot be assumed restorable (critical priority)\n- No DR site creates single point of failure (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Transportation CII operators face specific risks related to business continuity.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Undefined RTO/RPO prevents recovery objective validation", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for transportation"}, {"fact": "Untested backups cannot be assumed restorable", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for transportation"}, {"fact": "No DR site creates single point of failure", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for transportation"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - business continuity:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nBCP status: Plan exists, RTO undefined for critical systems, RPO undefined, Backups never tested, No DR site, Alternate workspace not arranged\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Undefined RTO/RPO prevents recovery objective validation (critical priority)\n- Untested backups cannot be assumed restorable (critical priority)\n- No DR site creates single point of failure (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Transportation CII operators face specific risks related to business continuity.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply transportation sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-012", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - data classification:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nData handling: All data treated same level, No classification labels, No encryption differentiation, Same access controls for all data types\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Unt differentiated protection wastes resources on low-value data (important priority)\n- Critical data may be under-protected without classification (critical priority)\n- Data classification is foundation for proportionate security (critical priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII operators face specific risks related to data classification.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Unt differentiated protection wastes resources on low-value data", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for banking"}, {"fact": "Critical data may be under-protected without classification", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for banking"}, {"fact": "Data classification is foundation for proportionate security", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for banking"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - data classification:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nData handling: All data treated same level, No classification labels, No encryption differentiation, Same access controls for all data types\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Unt differentiated protection wastes resources on low-value data (important priority)\n- Critical data may be under-protected without classification (critical priority)\n- Data classification is foundation for proportionate security (critical priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** Critical\n\n**Sector Context:** Banking CII operators face specific risks related to data classification.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply banking sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-013", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - change management:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nChange process: No approval required, No testing before production, No rollback capability, Changes undocumented, Emergency changes undefined\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Unapproved changes can inadvertently weaken security (critical priority)\n- No rollback capability prolongs outage duration (critical priority)\n- Undocumented changes prevent incident root cause analysis (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII operators face specific risks related to change management.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Unapproved changes can inadvertently weaken security", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for energy"}, {"fact": "No rollback capability prolongs outage duration", "tier": "critical", "source": "Configuration analysis for energy"}, {"fact": "Undocumented changes prevent incident root cause analysis", "tier": "important", "source": "Configuration analysis for energy"}], "expected_response": "**Risk Identification for Config analysis - change management:**\n\n**Configuration Analysis:**\nChange process: No approval required, No testing before production, No rollback capability, Changes undocumented, Emergency changes undefined\n\n**Identified Risks:**\n- Unapproved changes can inadvertently weaken security (critical priority)\n- No rollback capability prolongs outage duration (critical priority)\n- Undocumented changes prevent incident root cause analysis (important priority)\n\n\n**Risk Level:** High\n\n**Sector Context:** Energy CII operators face specific risks related to change management.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk assessment requirements", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze configuration", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply energy sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "risk_identification", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-014", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after MFA implementation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nMFA enabled for all admin access, MFA for remote access, Biometric MFA for data center\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nMFA bypass via token theft, MFA fatigue leading to approval habits, Session hijacking after authentication\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "MFA significantly reduces but does not eliminate credential theft risk", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for banking"}, {"fact": "Token theft and session hijacking remain viable attack vectors", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for banking"}, {"fact": "MFA fatigue can create approval automation risks", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for banking"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after MFA implementation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nMFA enabled for all admin access, MFA for remote access, Biometric MFA for data center\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nMFA bypass via token theft, MFA fatigue leading to approval habits, Session hijacking after authentication\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- MFA significantly reduces but does not eliminate credential theft risk (critical priority)\n- Token theft and session hijacking remain viable attack vectors (critical priority)\n- MFA fatigue can create approval automation risks (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply banking sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-015", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after network segmentation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nVLANs implemented, Firewalls between zones, DMZ for internet-facing systems, Microsegmentation for critical servers\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nCross-zone attacks via compromised applications, Firewall misconfiguration, Insider threats with legitimate access\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Segmentation limits but does not eliminate lateral movement", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for energy"}, {"fact": "Application-level attacks can bypass network controls", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for energy"}, {"fact": "Insiders with legitimate access are not mitigated by segmentation", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for energy"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after network segmentation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nVLANs implemented, Firewalls between zones, DMZ for internet-facing systems, Microsegmentation for critical servers\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nCross-zone attacks via compromised applications, Firewall misconfiguration, Insider threats with legitimate access\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Segmentation limits but does not eliminate lateral movement (critical priority)\n- Application-level attacks can bypass network controls (critical priority)\n- Insiders with legitimate access are not mitigated by segmentation (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply energy sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-016", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after encryption implementation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nAES-256 encryption at rest, TLS 1.3 for data in transit, Database encryption, Backup encryption\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nKey management vulnerabilities, Memory decryption attacks, Quantum computing future threat, Supply chain compromised encryption libraries\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Encryption protects data but key management remains critical", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for government"}, {"fact": "Decryption must happen in memory for use, creating exposure window", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for government"}, {"fact": "Compromised encryption implementation undermines protection", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for government"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after encryption implementation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nAES-256 encryption at rest, TLS 1.3 for data in transit, Database encryption, Backup encryption\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nKey management vulnerabilities, Memory decryption attacks, Quantum computing future threat, Supply chain compromised encryption libraries\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Encryption protects data but key management remains critical (critical priority)\n- Decryption must happen in memory for use, creating exposure window (important priority)\n- Compromised encryption implementation undermines protection (critical priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply government sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-017", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after SIEM deployment:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nComprehensive log collection, Real-time alerting, Correlation rules, 24/7 monitoring, 12-month retention\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nLegitimate activity indistinguishable from attack, Alert tuning creates blind spots, Dwell time before detection, Encrypted traffic analysis limits\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Monitoring detects but does not prevent attacks", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for telecommunications"}, {"fact": "Dwell time exists between compromise and detection", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for telecommunications"}, {"fact": "Over-tuned alerts reduce detection sensitivity", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for telecommunications"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after SIEM deployment:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nComprehensive log collection, Real-time alerting, Correlation rules, 24/7 monitoring, 12-month retention\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nLegitimate activity indistinguishable from attack, Alert tuning creates blind spots, Dwell time before detection, Encrypted traffic analysis limits\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Monitoring detects but does not prevent attacks (critical priority)\n- Dwell time exists between compromise and detection (critical priority)\n- Over-tuned alerts reduce detection sensitivity (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply telecommunications sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-018", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after patching program:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nMonthly vulnerability scanning, Quarterly patch cycle, Critical patching within 48 hours, OT risk-based patching\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nZero-day vulnerabilities unpatchable, Window between disclosure and patching, OT systems accept some risk for availability, Supply chain compromised patches\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Zero-day vulnerabilities cannot be addressed through patching", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for healthcare"}, {"fact": "Time window exists between vulnerability disclosure and patch availability", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for healthcare"}, {"fact": "OT risk acceptance necessary for operational availability", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for healthcare"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after patching program:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nMonthly vulnerability scanning, Quarterly patch cycle, Critical patching within 48 hours, OT risk-based patching\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nZero-day vulnerabilities unpatchable, Window between disclosure and patching, OT systems accept some risk for availability, Supply chain compromised patches\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Zero-day vulnerabilities cannot be addressed through patching (critical priority)\n- Time window exists between vulnerability disclosure and patch availability (critical priority)\n- OT risk acceptance necessary for operational availability (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply healthcare sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "medium", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-019", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after vendor management:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nVendor security assessments, Contractual security requirements, Right-to-audit clauses, Limited vendor access, Monitoring of vendor activity\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nVendor supply chain compromise, Vendor insider threats, Subcontractor risks not directly managed, Vendor dependency for remediation\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Vendor controls manage but do not eliminate supply chain risk", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for water"}, {"fact": "Subcontractor risks may be outside direct visibility", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for water"}, {"fact": "Vendor dependency creates availability risk", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for water"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after vendor management:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nVendor security assessments, Contractual security requirements, Right-to-audit clauses, Limited vendor access, Monitoring of vendor activity\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nVendor supply chain compromise, Vendor insider threats, Subcontractor risks not directly managed, Vendor dependency for remediation\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Vendor controls manage but do not eliminate supply chain risk (critical priority)\n- Subcontractor risks may be outside direct visibility (important priority)\n- Vendor dependency creates availability risk (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply water sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide §4.1"], "clause_reference_original": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "clause_reference_corrected_by": "agent-team-2026-04-26", "clause_reference_corrected_verdict": "ANNOTATOR_SUPERIOR_WITH_ONE_GAP"}}
{"test_id": "B09-020", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after incident response preparation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nDocumented IR plan, Tested procedures, Forensic capability, CSA reporting process, Communication plan\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nIncident still causes business impact, Evidence collection incomplete, Response time delays, Reputation damage despite good response\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "IR preparation reduces but does not prevent incident impact", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for transportation"}, {"fact": "Some damage always occurs before detection and response", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for transportation"}, {"fact": "Reputation impact independent of response quality", "tier": "supporting", "source": "Residual risk assessment for transportation"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after incident response preparation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nDocumented IR plan, Tested procedures, Forensic capability, CSA reporting process, Communication plan\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nIncident still causes business impact, Evidence collection incomplete, Response time delays, Reputation damage despite good response\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- IR preparation reduces but does not prevent incident impact (critical priority)\n- Some damage always occurs before detection and response (critical priority)\n- Reputation impact independent of response quality (supporting priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply transportation sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-021", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after security awareness training:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nAnnual training for all staff, Phishing simulations, Role-specific training, Security awareness materials\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nTraining decay over time, Sophisticated phishing bypasses awareness, Insider threats not addressed by training, Human error remains\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Training reduces human error but does not eliminate it", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for banking"}, {"fact": "Training effectiveness decays without reinforcement", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for banking"}, {"fact": "Insider threats not addressed by awareness training", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for banking"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after security awareness training:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nAnnual training for all staff, Phishing simulations, Role-specific training, Security awareness materials\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nTraining decay over time, Sophisticated phishing bypasses awareness, Insider threats not addressed by training, Human error remains\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Training reduces human error but does not eliminate it (critical priority)\n- Training effectiveness decays without reinforcement (important priority)\n- Insider threats not addressed by awareness training (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply banking sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-022", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after physical security upgrades:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nBadge access system, Biometric verification, Camera coverage, Security guards, Man-trap entry\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nTailgating and piggybacking, Badge theft, Guard collusion, Emergency exit bypass, Social engineering\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Physical security controls can be bypassed or defeated", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for energy"}, {"fact": "Social engineering exploits human aspects of security", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for energy"}, {"fact": "Insider threats have legitimate physical access", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for energy"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after physical security upgrades:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nBadge access system, Biometric verification, Camera coverage, Security guards, Man-trap entry\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nTailgating and piggybacking, Badge theft, Guard collusion, Emergency exit bypass, Social engineering\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Physical security controls can be bypassed or defeated (critical priority)\n- Social engineering exploits human aspects of security (critical priority)\n- Insider threats have legitimate physical access (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply energy sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-023", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after backup implementation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nDaily automated backups, Offsite storage, Encryption, Quarterly restoration tests, Versioned backups\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nRTO/RPO may not be met for large failures, Backup window data loss, Ransomware infects backups, Recovery process failures\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Backups enable recovery but do not guarantee recovery objectives", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for healthcare"}, {"fact": "Ransomware can infect backup if not properly isolated", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for healthcare"}, {"fact": "Data loss window exists between backup cycles", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for healthcare"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after backup implementation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nDaily automated backups, Offsite storage, Encryption, Quarterly restoration tests, Versioned backups\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nRTO/RPO may not be met for large failures, Backup window data loss, Ransomware infects backups, Recovery process failures\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Backups enable recovery but do not guarantee recovery objectives (critical priority)\n- Ransomware can infect backup if not properly isolated (critical priority)\n- Data loss window exists between backup cycles (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply healthcare sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-024", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after access control implementation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nLeast privilege enforcement, Regular access reviews, Role-based access control, Privileged access management, Session timeouts\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nPrivilege escalation vulnerabilities, Authorization bypass flaws, Session hijacking, Access review timing gaps, Broken access control in custom apps\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Access controls reduce but do not eliminate unauthorized access risk", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for government"}, {"fact": "Implementation flaws can undermine access control design", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for government"}, {"fact": "Time gap between reviews allows privilege creep", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for government"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after access control implementation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nLeast privilege enforcement, Regular access reviews, Role-based access control, Privileged access management, Session timeouts\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nPrivilege escalation vulnerabilities, Authorization bypass flaws, Session hijacking, Access review timing gaps, Broken access control in custom apps\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Access controls reduce but do not eliminate unauthorized access risk (critical priority)\n- Implementation flaws can undermine access control design (critical priority)\n- Time gap between reviews allows privilege creep (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply government sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
{"test_id": "B09-025", "version": "2.0", "benchmark_id": "B09", "input": {"question": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after penetration testing and remediation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nAnnual pen testing, Vulnerability scanning, Exploit remediation, Security controls implementation, Architecture review\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nNovel attack techniques not tested, Tester skill limitations, Testing window snapshot effect, Zero-day vulnerabilities, Human adaptation to bypasses new controls\n\n\n\nWhat are the key security risks or residual risks in this scenario?", "scenario_sector": "energy", "scenario_role": "risk_manager"}, "ground_truth": {"key_facts": [{"fact": "Pen testing validates controls against known attack patterns", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for telecommunications"}, {"fact": "Novel or zero-day attacks may not be identified", "tier": "critical", "source": "Residual risk assessment for telecommunications"}, {"fact": "Testing is point-in-time, not continuous validation", "tier": "important", "source": "Residual risk assessment for telecommunications"}], "expected_response": "**Residual Risk Assessment for Residual risk after penetration testing and remediation:**\n\n**Controls Implemented:**\nAnnual pen testing, Vulnerability scanning, Exploit remediation, Security controls implementation, Architecture review\n\n**Remaining Risks:**\nNovel attack techniques not tested, Tester skill limitations, Testing window snapshot effect, Zero-day vulnerabilities, Human adaptation to bypasses new controls\n\n**Residual Risk Analysis:**\n- Pen testing validates controls against known attack patterns (critical priority)\n- Novel or zero-day attacks may not be identified (critical priority)\n- Testing is point-in-time, not continuous validation (important priority)\n\n\n**Key Insight:** Security controls reduce but rarely eliminate risk. Understanding residual risk is essential for ongoing risk management and determining whether additional controls are cost-justified.\n\n**Risk Acceptance Consideration:** Whether residual risk is acceptable depends on sector context, regulatory requirements, and organizational risk appetite.\n\nReference: CCoP 2.0 risk management principles", "reasoning_chain": ["Analyze controls applied", "Identify security risks or remaining vulnerabilities", "Apply telecommunications sector context"]}, "fail_conditions": {"forbidden_claims": ["Stating controls eliminate all risk", "Downplaying critical risk severity", "Confusing different types of risk", "Clear identification of security risks or residual risks", "Sector-specific context consideration", "Assessment of risk severity or implications"], "hallucination_patterns": ["Inventing specific vulnerabilities not in scenario", "Creating non-existent residual risks"]}, "metadata": {"section": "3", "clause_reference": ["3.2.2(a)", "3.2.4", "3.2.5"], "domain": "IT", "difficulty": "high", "scenario_type": "residual_risk", "related_sections": [], "test_category": "edge_case", "created_date": "2026-04-01", "reviewer": null, "support_citations": ["Risk Assessment Guide \u00a74.1"]}}
